# =============================================================================
# .gitignore for CRRT-dose-lmtp
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A RULE.
#
# This repo is PRIVATE, and that changes what belongs in git relative to the
# sibling consortium repo (CLIF-epidemiology-of-CRRT), which is public-facing
# and therefore ignores `.claude`, `CLAUDE.md`, and `docs/`.
#
# Here those three are TRACKED ON PURPOSE:
#
#   .claude/   holds the LMTP feasibility findings, which are the entire
#              evidentiary basis for this project. They previously lived in
#              the sibling repo under `code/adhoc/` -- a gitignored path --
#              and so existed as exactly one untracked, unbacked-up copy.
#              This repo exists partly to fix that. Ignoring `.claude/` here
#              would silently recreate the problem.
#   CLAUDE.md  carries the inherited design decisions; memory is path-keyed
#              and does not follow the code, so this file is the durable copy.
#   docs/      deliverables the author reads. Untracked docs get lost.
#
# Do not "sync" this file with the sibling's. They are answering different
# questions. See CLAUDE.md > Repo conventions.
# =============================================================================

# --- Site configuration (never leaves the site) ------------------------------
config/config.json
config/config_*.json
!config/config_template.json

# --- Data: raw CLIF tables must never be committed ---------------------------
CLIF_*.parquet
CLIF_*.csv
CLIF_*.fst
*.RData

# --- Outputs -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Ignore output contents, keep the READMEs that explain the layout.
output/**
!output/README.md
!output/final_no_phi/
!output/final_no_phi/README.md
!output/intermediate_phi/
!output/intermediate_phi/README.md

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- R / renv ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Commit renv.lock, renv/activate.R and renv/settings.json; ignore only the
# local library. .Rprofile is intentionally NOT ignored: it sources
# renv/activate.R and must ship so every site uses the pinned library.
renv/library/
renv/local/
renv/staging/
renv/sandbox/
.Rhistory
.Ruserdata
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj

# --- Editors / OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Rendered artifacts ------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: deliberately NOT a blanket `*.pdf` / `*.html` ignore (the sibling repo
# has one). Figures and rendered reports are the product here, so only the
# transient R plot dump is excluded.
Rplots.pdf
